<title>CHINA: China '97 cotton output seen 4.0-4.15 mln T.</title>
<headline>China '97 cotton output seen 4.0-4.15 mln T.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's cotton output for 1997 was forecast at 4.0-4.15 million tonnes, compared with 4.2 million tonnes last year, the Futures Herald said on Thursday quoting a forecast by the Ministry of Internal Trade.  </p>
<p>The forecast attributed the expected smaller cotton crop to a reduction in planted acreage.</p>
<p>The area under cotton was estimated at 4.56 million hectares, the lowest level in a decade, the ministry said.</p>
<p>If no major natural disasters hit the crop, the maximum harvest for the year would be 4.15 million tonnes, it said.</p>
</text>
